  "id": "big-five-personality-model",
  "term": "Big Five personality model",
  "definition": "The Big Five personality model is a widely accepted dimensional way of describing personality in terms of five broad traits: neuroticism, conscientiousness, openness, agreeableness, and extraversion. In this view, personality refers to a person’s characteristic patterns of thinking, feeling, and behaving, and these traits have been linked to differences in well-being and work-related functioning.",
